* ============================================================================
* NAV ORDER NATURAL REGRESSION v1
*
* AIF-148. An ATTACHED CONTAINER IS NOT AN ACTIVE ORDER.
*
* orderstate::hasOrder() returns `st && !st->container.empty()` -- it answers
* "is a container attached". Six sites on the traversal path read it as "is an
* order active". WORKSPACE OPEN attaches a .cdx and selects NO TAG, so the
* predicate said true for a table sitting in natural order, and every verb
* that trusted it went looking for a tag, found none, and returned failure.
*
* MEASURED 2026-08-29 on MCC STUDENTS (200 rows, CDX attached, no tag):
*   TOP / BOTTOM / GO TOP / GO BOTTOM / GO FIRST / GO LAST -> "failed."
*   SKIP  -> "SKIP: at end."  on record 1, cursor did not move
*   GO 5  -> Recno: 5
* GO <n> survived because R121 already ruled addressing absolute and traversal
* filtered. SKIP is the severity: the other six REFUSED, which is a wrong
* answer you can see. SKIP ANSWERED.
*
* WHY SIXTY REGISTERED SPECS SAID NOTHING, measured 2026-08-29:
*   (a) 345 markers across the tracked corpus and NOT ONE mentions RECNO --
*       and that is not laziness, it is a language limit this house has
*       already recorded four times (cnx_persist_proof, cnx_realtime_*,
*       index_maintenance_failure_proof): RECNO() RENDERS EMPTY IN A "?"
*       MARKER, and STR() does not rescue it. So no arm in the tree can say
*       "the cursor is at 1".
*   (b) Every navigation line in the corpus is followed by a marker that
*       reads a FIELD, and USE/SELECT/CREATE have already parked the cursor
*       on record 1, so a failed TOP and a working TOP read identically.
*       workspace_load_shortfall.dts:149 is the shape exactly:
*           USE STUDENTS / TOP / ? "L_T4...:" + (SID >= 1)
*       -- green from record 1 and green from record 400.
*   (c) STOP_ON_ERROR is opt-in, so "TOP: failed." prints above green markers
*       and the run continues.
*
* SO EVERY ARM HERE PARKS THE CURSOR SOMEWHERE ELSE FIRST and asserts by
* FIELD VALUE, never by RECNO() and never by console text. An arm that reads
* row 1 on a table already standing on row 1 cannot fail, which is the whole
* reason this defect lived.
*
* THE FIXTURE SORTS BACKWARDS ON PURPOSE. ID descends as the physical order
* ascends, so natural order and tag order name DIFFERENT rows. Without that a
* fix that forced everything to natural would read green here, and forcing
* natural is as wrong as refusing.
*
*   physical 1 2 3 4 5 6   ->  MARK ROW1 ROW2 ROW3 ROW4 ROW5 ROW6
*   ID       60 50 40 30 20 10
*   natural TOP -> ROW1        tag(ID asc) TOP -> ROW6
*
* SMARTLIST, not LIST, for every transcript dump (owner, 2026-08-29: "list is
* my tool, use smartlist for tests").
*
* AND SMARTLIST MOVES THE CURSOR -- its own header says so, "mutates: cursor",
* where LIST restores best-effort. So a dump is never allowed to sit between a
* park and its assertion; both dumps here are followed by an explicit GO <n>.
* This is the same trap as (b) above wearing different clothes: a spec that
* listed a table and then asserted on "where the cursor is" would be reading
* the listing, not the verb.
*
* Self-bootstrapping in SANDBOX, self-erasing. Mints no catalog rows: the
* attached-no-tag state is reached with SET INDEX TO (cmd_setindex.cpp:237-239
* sets the container and then setActiveTag(A, "")), which is the same state
* WORKSPACE OPEN produces via attach_workspace_index (cmd_workspace.cpp:1123-
* 1130) without needing a workspace to produce it.
*
*   Standalone:  DO nav_order_natural_regression
*   Regression:  REGRESSION RUN NAV_NATURAL
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO NAV ORDER NATURAL REGRESSION v1
ECHO ============================================================

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/SANDBOX
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/SANDBOX
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE navtag CONFIRM

FORMULA "NAV-NATURAL-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- the fixture -------------------------------------------------------------
SELECT 0
CREATE X64 NAVTAG (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 60
REPLACE MARK WITH "ROW1"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 50
REPLACE MARK WITH "ROW2"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 40
REPLACE MARK WITH "ROW3"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 30
REPLACE MARK WITH "ROW4"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 20
REPLACE MARK WITH "ROW5"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 10
REPLACE MARK WITH "ROW6"

ECHO
ECHO --- the fixture, physical order ---
SMARTLIST ID,MARK

* --- G0/G1: the fixture and the PARK both work -------------------------------
* G1 IS NOT CEREMONY. Every arm below parks with GO <n> and then reads MARK.
* If GO does not move, an arm that reads ROW1 after TOP proves nothing at all,
* because the cursor never left ROW1. G1 is the arm that makes the other arms
* mean something, and it is asserted on a row that is NEITHER first NOR last.
GO 1
? "NAV_G0_fixture_row1_written:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW1")
GO 4
? "NAV_G1_park_moved_off_row1:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW4")
GO 6
? "NAV_G2_park_reaches_last_row:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW6")

* --- build the container -----------------------------------------------------
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG ID
BUILDLMDB

* --- THE STATE UNDER TEST: ATTACHED, NO TAG ----------------------------------
* SET INDEX TO attaches the container and clears the active tag. This is the
* same state WORKSPACE OPEN leaves every table it lands in, reached without
* opening a workspace so this spec mints nothing.
SET INDEX TO navtag

ECHO
ECHO --- attached, no tag: STATUS should read NATURAL with the file named ---
STATUS
* Expect: Order: NATURAL / Index file: ...navtag.cdx / Active tag: (none).
* NOT ASSERTED -- markers in this language compare field values, never console
* text (FIELDMGR_APPEND doctrine). Stated so a reader does not credit the arms
* below with having checked it.

ECHO
ECHO --- G3: addressing still works with the container attached ---
* R121: GO <n> is absolute and was never broken. If this reds, the fixture or
* the attach is wrong and every arm below is unproven.
GO 4
? "NAV_G3_addressing_survives_attach:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW4")

* --- ARM 1: TOP ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Parked on ROW4. Pre-fix: "TOP: failed.", cursor stays, MARK reads ROW4, .F.
GO 4
TOP
? "NAV_T1_top_reaches_first_physical:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW1")

* --- ARM 2: BOTTOM ------------------------------------------------------------
GO 1
BOTTOM
? "NAV_T2_bottom_reaches_last_physical:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW6")

* --- ARM 3: SKIP FORWARD -- THE ONE THAT LIED ---------------------------------
* Pre-fix this printed "SKIP: at end." on record 1 of 6 and did not move, so
* the arm reads ROW1 and goes red. The other six verbs refused out loud; this
* one answered, which is why it leads the finding.
GO 1
SKIP
? "NAV_T3_skip_forward_moved_one_row:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW2")

* --- ARM 4: SKIP BACKWARD -----------------------------------------------------
GO 6
SKIP -1
? "NAV_T4_skip_backward_moved_one_row:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW5")

* --- ARM 5/6: THE GO FORMS ----------------------------------------------------
* GO TOP and GO BOTTOM route differently from bare TOP/BOTTOM and failed
* separately in the 2026-08-29 transcript ("GO: failed." x4), so they are
* separate arms rather than assumed to follow.
GO 4
GO TOP
? "NAV_T5_go_top_reaches_first_physical:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW1")
GO 1
GO BOTTOM
? "NAV_T6_go_bottom_reaches_last_physical:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW6")

* --- ARM 7/8: A TAG IS ACTIVE -- NATURAL MUST NOT WIN -------------------------
* THE COUNTERWEIGHT ARMS. Everything above asserts that a tagless container
* falls back to natural. A fix that forced natural ALWAYS would pass all six
* and be just as wrong, so these two assert the opposite direction on the same
* fixture: with tag ID active, ascending, TOP is the LOWEST ID, which is
* physical row 6.
SET ORDER TO TAG ID

ECHO
ECHO --- tag order, which must not match physical ---
SMARTLIST ID,MARK

GO 1
TOP
? "NAV_T7_tag_top_follows_the_tag:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW6")
GO 1
BOTTOM
? "NAV_T8_tag_bottom_follows_the_tag:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "ROW1")

* --- WHAT THIS SPEC DOES NOT COVER, stated rather than implied ----------------
* (a) The REPORT sites that still read the container predicate where they make
*     an ordering claim: status_helpers.cpp:28, index_summary.cpp:170,
*     db_tuple_stream.cpp:483, cmd_workspace.cpp:4587. Console text, and no
*     marker in this language can assert it.
* (b) GO FIRST / GO LAST. They failed alongside GO TOP/GO BOTTOM in the same
*     transcript and are believed to share the path, but believed is not
*     measured and they are not armed here.
* (c) A FILTERED view. cmd_skip.cpp's fast-path guard pairs the order question
*     with view_is_filtered() deliberately (R121); this spec exercises the
*     unfiltered half only.
* (d) CNX. The predicate treats .cnx and .cdx alike (container_supports_tag),
*     so the CNX arm should behave identically -- untested, unclaimed.

* --- CLEANUP ------------------------------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE navtag CONFIRM
* The navtag.cdx and its LMDB sidecar live under the SANDBOX index/lmdb slots
* and are erased with the table.

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO NAV ORDER NATURAL REGRESSION v1 DONE
ECHO ============================================================
